## Multi-tab fixes (shared state across panels)

Current: each tab mounts own `GitDiffPanel` w/ own poll, snapshot, parse, tokenize. Hidden tabs stay mounted (`display:none`). Two tabs on same worktree → 2× everything.

| # | Fix | Mechanism | Impact |
|---|-----|-----------|--------|
| M1 | Shared snapshot cache keyed by `(targetPath, params)` | Module-level Map + refcount subscribers (SWR-style) | High |
| M2 | Main-process fs watcher per worktree → push updates | `chokidar` on `.git/index` + worktree; IPC broadcast | High |
| M3 | Global tokenize cache (content-hash → HlSpan[][]) | LRU across all panels/tabs | Med |
| M4 | Single shared Worker (pool of 1-2) across all panels | Worker module singleton | Med |
| M5 | Global parsed-diff cache (patch string → FileDiff[]) | WeakMap/LRU, dedup across tabs | Med |
| M6 | Unmount (or hard-pause) panels for hidden tabs | Verify `visible` prop truly false on `display:none` | Low |
| M7 | Stagger/batch polls per worktree | Coordinator flushes once per interval | Low (obsolete if M2) |
| M8 | Share untracked-file diffs cache across tabs | Same map as M5 | Low |

## Recommended multi-tab arch

Single source of truth per worktree:

```
main: GitWatcher(worktreePath) → chokidar(.git/index, .git/HEAD, tree)
         ↓ debounced change event
      compute snapshot once
         ↓ IPC broadcast
renderer: useGitDiff(targetPath) subscribes, shares parsed + tokenized data
```

- Removes polling entirely (M2)
- One snapshot per worktree, N subscribers (M1)
- Parse + tokenize once, cached globally (M3/M5)
- Tabs on same worktree → near-zero marginal cost

## Implementation order

1. **A + C** — virtualize file list + worker tokenize (~90% of per-panel stall)
2. **M1 + M5** — renderer-only shared caches, dedup across tabs
3. **B** — line virtualization for huge files
4. **M3 + M4** — global worker + tokenize cache
5. **E, G** — parse memo + drop full-ctx fetch
6. **M2** — fs watcher replaces polling (separate PR, touches main)
7. **M6, D, I, H, K, J, M7, M8** — polish

## Notes

- A + C + M3 + M4 compose well: virtualized list → worker → global cache
- G trade-off: context toggle requires re-fetch (cheap, acceptable)
- I threshold tunable; log when highlight disabled
- F obsolete if M2 ships
- M6: verify `visible` prop actually false for hidden tabs — cheap bug check
